@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Class Diagram - Classroom Quiz

class Teacher
class Student
class Group {
  groupName
}
class Activity {
  phase : ready | active | completed | ended
  stateVersion
  openRoundIdsByQuestion
  createdAt
  endedAt
}
class Question {
  questionNumber
  prompt
  kind : single | group
}
class Round {
  phase
  openedAt
  closedAt
  nextOrder
  publishedAnswer (after a successful writeback)
}
class Submission {
  answers[]
  acceptedOrder
}
class GuidedNotesSheet {
  worksheetName
  structureFingerprint
}
class AnswerSlot {
  label
  prompt
  mappingStatus
}
class ActivityEvent {
  stateVersion
  eventType
}
class WritebackJob {
  status
  attempt
  claimedAt
  adoptedSource : group | teacher
  adoptedGroupId
  answers[]
  revision
}

Teacher "1" --> "0..*" Activity : controls (listed in 我的課堂活動 via teacher:{id}:activities)
Activity "1" *-- "1..*" Question : contains
Activity "1" *-- "0..*" Round : runs (several may be open at once)
Round "0..1" --> "1" Question : opens (once per question)
Student "0..*" --> "1" Group : joins as
Group "1" --> "0..*" Submission : submits
Round "1" --> "0..*" Submission : receives
Question "1" --> "0..*" Submission : answered by
GuidedNotesSheet "1" --> "1..*" Question : imports by question number
Question "1" *-- "1..*" AnswerSlot : maps dynamically (one per sub-question)
Activity "1" --> "0..*" ActivityEvent : appends versioned events
Round "1" --> "0..1" WritebackJob : writes the adopted answer after close

note right of Submission
  Rank each group by its first accepted answer.
  The fastest answer is preselected, but the teacher adopts
  the answer that is written back (any group or a typed answer).
  Students only ever see their own answer plus the adopted one.
  Order and winner are kept per round, so rounds
  that are open at the same time never affect each other.
end note
note bottom of AnswerSlot
  Resolve from the header row, question number and sheet content.
  Never depend on fixed cell coordinates.
  A group question has one slot per sub-question; a submission
  carries one answer per slot and must fill all of them.
end note

@enduml
